f-my-time-clive-james"}],"publicationYear":2007,"pageCount":918,"summary":"‘In the forty years it took me to write this book, I only gradually realized that the finished work, if it were going to be true to the pattern of my experience, would have no pattern . . . The book I wanted to write had its origins in the books I was reading. Several times, in my early days, I had to sell my best books to buy food, so I never underlined anything. When conditions improved I became less fastidious. Not long after I began marking passages for future consideration, I also began keeping notes in the margin beside the markings, and then longer notes on the endpapers . . . As the time for assembling my reflections approached, I resolved that a premature synthesis was the thing to be avoided. So this is a book about how not to reach one. If I have done my job properly, themes will emerge from the apparent randomness and make this work intelligible.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2388550-L.jpg","renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":54,"criticalRenown":72,"controversy":12,"llmAffinity":86,"affinityResidual":5.57,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.92,"criticalRenown":0.9,"controversy":0.82,"llmAffinity":0.98},"tags":{"craft":"prose-style","evidence":"synthesis-of-scholarship","stance":"wonder"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Premature synthesis should be avoided so that themes can emerge from apparent randomness and make experience intelligible.","confidence":0.86},"academicOrientation":{"score":35,"confidence":0.78},"profileConfidence":0.88,"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"b2458a2255a66760fe5c5e650febe3466b6e5c32ff5bde12d9d21455838eeaa0","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"displaySummary":"The book I wanted to write had its origins in the books I was reading. Several times, in my early days, I had to se